hi there steve kaufman here uh talking  to you again  about my great passion which is language  learning  um  if you enjoy these videos um please  subscribe  uh i do feel strongly that anyone can  learn languages  one foreign language several foreign  languages and i try to encourage people  to to do so and provide some  advice from my own experience  so today i want to talk about the idea  that  with a relatively limited vocabulary we  can actually  communicate quite effectively in in a  language in a foreign language  um  you know it is known that a relatively  small number of words  say a thousand words will account for  70  depending on you know the context 60 70  75 percent of any given  language content so if we just learn  those 1000 words uh we can then uh do  quite well in the language that's the  theory  i have never found that to be the case  okay so up front i'll give you the  conclusion  not true  uh for a variety of reasons  first of all  i just the reason i'm  you know wanting to talk about this is  because i was noticing that in my arabic  now i have 1100 known words the way we  count words at link  now granted uh you know in arabic  there's different forms of verbs and  nouns and they tack the and onto  nouns and so  you know this number in terms of word  families would be quite a bit lower  so it's not totally indicative but it's  a beginning of an indication of just how  much you can cover with a limited  vocabulary so  i have 1100 known words  probably it's a bit higher but let's say  it's 1100 known words  as identified by link by the system  so if i open a new lesson  in the many stories series we have 60  many stories in arabic the same many  stories that i used for greek and i love  them they're addictive they cover  mostly the most common vocabulary in  particular the most common verbs which i  think is very important so it's not you  know real authentic content  but  and there's a lot of repetition in them  but if i open a news story  even though i know 1100 words  typically there's 35 to 40 percent  unknown words in those lessons unknown  to me  unknown to me means i haven't come  across them before in our system  if i open a lesson from let's learn  arabic which is still material that is  designed for learners but it's a little  more difficult  and it's a different series so a  different vocabulary there i'm looking  at 50 unknown words  if i open  because that link we have this news feed  so i can get you know uh articles from  huffington post in arabic or whatever  happens to feed into my feed  there there's 60 unknown words so i have  1100 known words but these  lessons either you know learner material  showing me 40 unknown words  intermediate level material 50 unknown  words news articles 60  unknown words in other words in other  words  having 1100 known words doesn't enable  me  to understand these articles  there are still lots of words that i  don't know  and you know it's true for example  typically in the sort of beginner books  where they promise that you will master  this language  and they take you to you know the  customs and the doctor and the bank and  therefore now you know this vocabulary  it doesn't work that way because even if  you think you know  a thousand words  when you need them you probably won't  remember them or there's a good chance  you know how many times  have i looked i need to know the word  for such and such because i don't know  i'm going to the store to buy this  uh two problems with that probably i  will forget the word by the time i get  to the store it's happened to me so  often  or  because we have no way of anticipating  what that person in the store is going  to say what words they're going to use  um  that word may not even the words that i  think i now have mastered that are going  to enable me to navigate this instant  this situation  in fact there might be a whole new range  of words that come come up so  the conclusion is  the idea that you can somehow focus in  on a small number of words and then be  comfortable in the language is simply  not true  beyond that because  the best way to get used to a language  is to do a lot of listening and reading  you can't stay forever with  content that only has these you know  most frequent 1000 words you have to get  into other words  and  the less frequent words of course they  appear less frequently so they're more  difficult to learn and therefore you  have to consume massive quantities of  material before these words sink in but  as you are pursuing  this is my i always sort of make  reference to this sort of  you know  dog races where the dogs chase the  mechanical rabbit  as i am chasing  these new words and trying to increase  my vocabulary on link at the same time  i'm going over again and again and again  the words that i already know the  structures that i have already met i'm  becoming familiar with the language so  that  those even the high frequency words i'm  not learning them as a deliberate task  with lists  i am absorbing them naturally so that  they become a comfortable part of me and  that's one of the reasons by the way  that i really recommend using our many  stories we have them in a variety of  languages  linked because  they're good to get started in a  language i use them for greek i'm using  them for arabic  but i want to go back and do russian in  many stories and and check many stories  because  it's an opportunity to go over some of  the basic structures and the basic  vocabulary because there's always things  that slip all these things that we lose  and that's why we need to have this  massive exposure and you can't just go  in there and try to isolate  a small number of very high frequency  words and hope to achieve anything close  to  fluency or even  any level of comfort in the language so  there you have it i look forward to your  comments bye for now  [Music]  you
 

